From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tfrecomp <tfrecomp@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:24:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] native: no warning per Present() for the missing frame
 latency semaphore

There are no Win32 semaphores in a native build: CreateSemaphore() is a
stub that returns null, so the swap chain's frame latency semaphore is
null and IDXGISwapChain2::GetFrameLatencyWaitableObject() returns null.
The swap chain still calls ReleaseSemaphore() on it for every Present(),
and the stub logged a warning each time: one line per frame on stderr
and in the log file.  Keep the warning for a non-null handle only.
---
 src/util/util_win32_compat.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/util/util_win32_compat.h b/src/util/util_win32_compat.h
index e4a556a..a14ff80 100644
--- a/src/util/util_win32_compat.h
+++ b/src/util/util_win32_compat.h
@@ -78,7 +78,10 @@ inline HANDLE CreateSemaphore(LPSECURITY_ATTRIBUTES lpSemaphoreAttributes,
 inline BOOL ReleaseSemaphore(HANDLE hSemaphore,
                              LONG   lReleaseCount,
                              LPLONG lpPreviousCount) {
-  dxmt::Logger::warn("ReleaseSemaphore not implemented.");
+  // A swap chain releases its frame latency semaphore on every Present().
+  // CreateSemaphore() above gives it a null one: do not warn once per frame.
+  if (hSemaphore)
+    dxmt::Logger::warn("ReleaseSemaphore not implemented.");
   return FALSE;
 }
 
